cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use interpreTFM, please cite it as below. A manuscript describing the
  method is in preparation; this file will point to it once it is published.
title: "interpreTFM: layer-resolved evaluation of transcriptomic foundation models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hu
    given-names: Yunfei
version: 0.9.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/OliiverHu/interpreTFM"
url: "https://interpretfm.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  interpreTFM is a layer-resolved framework for evaluating what transcriptomic
  foundation models (scGPT, Geneformer and C2S-Scale) encode, using sparse
  autoencoders, on single-cell and targeted spatial transcriptomic data. It
  provides the transcriptomic interpretability score, held-out concept alignment
  against raw hidden dimensions and untrained sparse autoencoders, cell-level
  feature tables, and building blocks for spatial niche and interface analysis.
keywords:
  - transcriptomic foundation models
  - sparse autoencoders
  - interpretability
  - single-cell
  - spatial transcriptomics
